  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: bfcb709b487afd749b8fbd2c4c50e261, type: 3}
  m_Name: Paladin
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  Key: Paladin
  Label: Paladin
  Blurb: Armoured, patient, and certain. Holds a line, or breaks one, or mends it.
  Vision:
    Fantasy: 'An armoured believer. Holy power in service of the line: holds it,
      breaks it, or mends it.'
    Role: Front line with holy damage and healing. Attacks with Strength; heals scale
      off Spirit.
    SignatureMechanic: Some way of granting temporary invulnerability later on?
    UltraStyle: Divine aid
    Ultras:
    - Name: Divine Intervention
      Effect: Prime yourself and prevent the next physical (non magical) damage dealt
        from hitting the target, taking it instead at an extra 50% damage reduction.
        Afterwards retaliate with holy damage.
      Unlock: Tank branch early.
    Branches:
    - GridBranch: a
      Becomes: A front-liner who protects by drawing the enemy's attention.
      IntendedKit: Shield Up -> Ward
      Summon: 'Aegis Lion - special attack: +50% own Endurance for 3 turns and +60
        threat (a taunt).'
    - GridBranch: b
      Becomes: A holy damage dealer.
      IntendedKit: Sunder -> Consecrate
      Summon: 'Judgement Seraph - party replacement, a hitter: 120% HP / 180% STR,
        Radiant Cut and Judgement (Holy).'
    - GridBranch: c
      Becomes: A healer.
      IntendedKit: Heal -> Renew
      Summon: 'Dawn Stag - special attack: heals 40% of each hero''s health, then
        regeneration for 3 turns.'
    Overlaps: 'Warrior (front-liner, damage) and Cleric (healer). Three branches
      against their two: broader, never the best at any one.'
    OpenQuestions: What does a Paladin do that the Warrior and the Cleric cannot?
      Holy damage only so far.
